---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE } from '../../data/site';

const title = 'ZZZ Pull Economy – Budget for a Guaranteed Agent';
const description =
  'Zenless Zone Zero pull economy explained: realistic f2p income per patch, what a 50/50 and a guarantee cost, and how to budget polychromes with the pull planner.';
const updated = SITE.lastVerified;
---

<Base
  title={title}
  description={description}
  crumbs={[{ name: 'Guides' }, { name: 'Pull Economy Basics' }]}
  schema={[{
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'Article',
    headline: 'Zenless Zone Zero pull economy basics',
    datePublished: '2026-10-08',
    dateModified: updated,
    author: { '@type': 'Organization', name: SITE.brand },
  }]}
>
  <div class="page-head">
    <h1>Pull economy basics</h1>
    <div class="h1-bar"></div>
    <p class="lede">
      Agents are math before they are meta. Here's how to know — before a banner drops — whether your account
      can afford the worst case, and what "saving for a guarantee" actually means in polychromes.
    </p>
    <div class="microline"><span>By {SITE.brand}</span><span>Updated {updated}</span></div>
  </div>

  <section class="prose">
    <h2>Quick answer</h2>
    <p>
      A guaranteed rate-up S-rank costs at most 180 pulls' worth of currency (90 pity × 2 if the 50/50 loses);
      the expected cost is far lower. Budget for the worst case, treat anything less as profit, and run your
      exact pity through the <a href="/pull-planner/">pull planner</a> — it converts your position into odds and a currency number.
    </p>

    <h2>The three costs</h2>
    <div class="table-scroll">
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th>Outcome</th><th>Worst-case pulls</th><th>What it means</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Lucky 50/50 win</td><td class="mono">1 – 90</td><td>The dream; usually early-pity luck</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Lose 50/50, win guarantee</td><td class="mono">up to 180</td><td>The number your budget must survive</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Expected (model average)</td><td class="mono">~107 per rate-up</td><td>What long-run averages say [model estimate]</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <h2>Income rules of thumb</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Dailies + events are the floor.</strong> Login-and-clear play accrues a steady trickle per patch [NEEDS DATA for exact per-patch figures — track your own income].</li>
      <li><strong>Track your own account.</strong> Your pull history is the only honest income model; the planner's browser-only storage keeps a running tally without any account link.</li>
      <li><strong>F2P supports roughly one guaranteed S-rank per patch</strong> when nothing is banked — two if you skipped the previous banner. Treat that as the planning ceiling, not a promise.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Budget workflow</h2>
    <ol class="steps">
      <li>Enter pity and guarantee status in the <a href="/pull-planner/">pull planner</a>.</li>
      <li>Read the polychrome number — that's your worst-case reserve for this banner.</li>
      <li>Subtract what you actually hold; the gap is what dailies and events must cover before the banner ends.</li>
      <li>If the gap is unwinnable, decide now: skip and bank the guarantee, or accept a 50/50.</li>
    </ol>
  </section>
</Base>
